IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Academy of Law Act 1988 (Singapore) -- who is a member of the Academy and who a Fellow (ss 11, 12, 14), who is
-- disqualified, suspended or restored (s 16), the late-subscription interest (s 17), termination (s 18), who may sit on the Senate
-- as an appointed member (s 5(2), (3)), Senate quorum and votes (s 9), the Law Society nominee on committees (s 10(5), (6)), the
-- auditor-obstruction offence (s 22(7)) and the bar on actions against the Academy (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SALA1988.txt. The deposit's cover says it
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and is marked "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from
-- 17/4/2025"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 37 of 2023 wef 17/04/2025 (lawyers (NP)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0206 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. For an individual the answer is mostly membership: every Singapore lawyer, legal officer and registered
-- foreign lawyer is a member by force of s 14, pays a subscription and cannot sue over the Senate's official acts. SCOPED to that.
-- Not encoded: the Academy's functions and powers (s 4, including notaries public and document authentication, which are conferred
-- here but regulated elsewhere), the Senate's general powers and employment (ss 7, 8), accounts and financial statements (ss 19-21),
-- the auditor's duties (s 22(1)-(6)), tax exemption (s 23), the seal (s 24), recovery of debts (s 25) and rule-making (s 27).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was
-- not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Academy of Law Act 1988 -- membership`

DECLARE Person HAS
    `admitted as an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `admitted only ad hoc` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `admitted as a lawyer (NP)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Judicial Service, Legal Service or PD Officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registered or approved foreign lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected an honorary or associate member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `struck off the roll` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reinstated to the roll` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed from the service for misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `foreign registration or approval cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed from a law school for misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of an offence involving fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `mentally disordered and incapable of managing affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a composition or deed of arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `membership terminated by the Senate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `suspended from practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred by order from applying for admission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `president or vice-president` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an ex officio Senate member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years in high office since 1 January 1980` IS A NUMBER
    `appointed Senior Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected a Fellow` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `16(1), (4), (4A) -- disqualification and reinstatement`

-- s 16(1): "A person is not qualified to be a member of the Academy or, if he or she is a member, ceases to be a member if --
-- (a) he or she has been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors or roll of lawyers (NP); (b) being a Judicial Service
-- Officer, a Legal Service Officer or a PD Officer, he or she has been dismissed ... for misconduct in his or her professional
-- capacity; (c) being a foreign lawyer ... his or her registration ... or approval ... is cancelled; (d) [dismissed from the NUS,
-- SMU or SUSS law school] for misconduct ...; (e) he or she has been convicted of an offence involving fraud or dishonesty;
-- (f) he or she has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing himself or herself or his or her affairs; (g) he or she is an
-- undischarged bankrupt; or (h) he or she has entered into a composition with his or her creditors or a deed of arrangement".
-- (4), (4A): a member struck off "on being reinstated to the roll ... becomes a member of the Academy".
-- Reading (an inference): reinstatement cures paragraph (a) only; any other paragraph still disqualifies.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified` IF
        (`the person`'s `struck off the roll` AND (NOT `the person`'s `reinstated to the roll`))
    OR  `the person`'s `dismissed from the service for misconduct`
    OR  `the person`'s `foreign registration or approval cancelled`
    OR  `the person`'s `dismissed from a law school for misconduct`
    OR  `the person`'s `convicted of an offence involving fraud or dishonesty`
    OR  `the person`'s `mentally disordered and incapable of managing affairs`
    OR  `the person`'s `an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the person`'s `in a composition or deed of arrangement with creditors`

§§ `14 -- ordinary members, without election`

-- s 14: every person who "(a) is admitted as an advocate and solicitor, whether or not he or she has in force a practising
-- certificate ...; (aa) is admitted as a lawyer (NP) ...; (b) is a Judicial Service Officer, Legal Service Officer or PD Officer; or
-- (c) being a foreign lawyer -- (i) is registered under section 36B or 36D ... or (ii) is granted approval under section 176(1) ...
-- becomes, by virtue of this section and without election, admission or appointment by the Senate, an ordinary member of the Academy
-- unless he or she is disqualified ... under section 16 or his or her membership has been terminated under section 18."
-- s 2: "advocate and solicitor" ... "excludes any person admitted ad hoc under section 15 of the Legal Profession Act 1966".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an ordinary member` IF
        (    (`the person`'s `admitted as an advocate and solicitor` AND (NOT `the person`'s `admitted only ad hoc`))
         OR  `the person`'s `admitted as a lawyer (NP)`
         OR  `the person`'s `a Judicial Service, Legal Service or PD Officer`
         OR  `the person`'s `a registered or approved foreign lawyer`)
    AND (NOT `the person is disqualified` `the person`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `membership terminated by the Senate`)

-- ss 13, 15: the Senate may elect honorary and associate members. They too are subject to s 16 (an inference from "a person is not
-- qualified to be a member" in s 16(1), which is not limited to ordinary members).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member other than as a Fellow` IF
        `the person is an ordinary member` `the person`
    OR  (    `the person`'s `elected an honorary or associate member`
         AND (NOT `the person is disqualified` `the person`)
         AND (NOT `the person`'s `membership terminated by the Senate`))

§§ `12 -- Fellows`

-- s 12: the Fellows are "(a) the president and vice-presidents ...; (b) all other members of the Senate except for those appointed
-- under section 5(1)(h); (c) persons who have since 1 January 1980 held office as Chief Justice, Judge of the Supreme Court, Supreme
-- Court Judge, Attorney-General, Deputy Attorney-General or Solicitor-General for at least 2 years; (d) honorary or associate members
-- who are elected by the Senate as Fellows ...; and (e) members who have been appointed as Senior Counsel".
-- Paragraph (d) reaches only honorary and associate members; (e) only those already members. s 16 is applied to Fellows too (an
-- inference: s 2 says "member" includes a Fellow).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Fellow` IF
        (    `the person`'s `president or vice-president`
         OR  `the person`'s `an ex officio Senate member`
         OR  `the person`'s `years in high office since 1 January 1980` AT LEAST 2
         OR  (`the person`'s `elected a Fellow` AND `the person`'s `elected an honorary or associate member`)
         OR  (`the person`'s `appointed Senior Counsel` AND `the person is a member other than as a Fellow` `the person`))
    AND (NOT `the person is disqualified` `the person`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member` IF
        `the person is a member other than as a Fellow` `the person`
    OR  `the person is a Fellow` `the person`

§§ `16(3), (3A) -- suspension`

-- s 16(3): "Where a member of the Academy has been suspended from practising as an advocate and solicitor for any period, his or her
-- membership is deemed to be suspended for the duration of his or her suspension." (3A): likewise while subject to an order
-- "prohibiting him or her from applying to the court for admission ... until after a date specified in the order".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the membership is suspended` IF
        `the person is a member` `the person`
    AND (`the person`'s `suspended from practice` OR `the person`'s `barred by order from applying for admission`)

§§ `5(2), (3) -- appointed members of the Senate`

-- s 5(2): "A person must not be appointed as a member of the Senate pursuant to subsection (1)(h) unless he or she is a member of the
-- Academy and a citizen of Singapore." (3): the term is one year, with eligibility for re-appointment.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be appointed to the Senate under section 5(1)(h)` IF
    `the person is a member` `the person` AND `a citizen`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of an appointed Senate member in years` MEANS 1

§§ `5(1), 9(2)-(4) -- Senate size, quorum and votes`

-- s 5(1): the Senate is the Chief Justice, "the Supreme Court Judges", the Attorney-General, "every Deputy Attorney-General", the
-- Solicitor-General, the president of the Law Society, the Deans of the NUS, SMU and SUSS law schools (3), and "9 other members"
-- appointed by the Chief Justice. Its size therefore moves with the number of Judges and Deputy Attorneys-General.
-- (Counting the Chief Justice separately from "the Supreme Court Judges" is an inference; s 2 says "Supreme Court Judge" includes a
-- Judicial Commissioner.)
GIVEN `number of Supreme Court Judges` IS A NUMBER, `number of Deputy Attorneys-General` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the size of the Senate` MEANS
    1 PLUS `number of Supreme Court Judges` PLUS 1 PLUS `number of Deputy Attorneys-General` PLUS 1 PLUS 1 PLUS 3 PLUS 9

-- s 9(2): "A majority of the members of the Senate constitutes a quorum". (3): questions are decided "by a majority of the votes of
-- the members present". (4): the presiding member "has a deliberative vote and has, in the event of an equality of votes, a casting
-- vote". (6): vacancies do not invalidate proceedings (whether a vacancy reduces the quorum count is not said; not modelled).
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `Senate size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `Senate size`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the chair casts for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
    IF `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `votes for` EQUALS `votes against` THEN `the chair casts for`
         ELSE FALSE

§§ `10(5), (6) -- the Law Society nominee on every committee or board`

-- s 10(5): every committee or board "must have among its members at least one person who -- (a) is a practising advocate and
-- solicitor; (b) has, for an aggregate period of 7 years, been one or more of ... a practising advocate and solicitor ... a Judicial
-- Service Officer ... a Legal Service Officer; and (c) is nominated by the Council of the Law Society." (6): "Subsection (5) does not
-- apply if one of the members of the committee or board is a member of the Council of the Law Society."
GIVEN `nominee practising` IS A BOOLEAN, `nominee aggregate years` IS A NUMBER, `nominated by the Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Council member sits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee is properly constituted` IF
        `a Council member sits`
    OR  (`nominee practising` AND `nominee aggregate years` AT LEAST 7 AND `nominated by the Council`)

§§ `17 -- annual subscription and interest`

-- s 17(1): "Every member must pay to the Academy an annual subscription of an amount determined by the Senate". (3): "If any member
-- fails to pay his or her annual subscription within 30 days of the subscription becoming due, he or she must pay interest (if any)
-- at the rate determined by the Senate." (4): "The Senate may waive the subscription payable by any member".
-- Reading (an inference): paying on day 30 after the due date is "within 30 days".
GIVEN `days after the due date` IS A NUMBER, `the Senate set an interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the subscription was waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `interest is payable on the subscription` IF
        `days after the due date` GREATER THAN 30
    AND `the Senate set an interest rate`
    AND (NOT `the subscription was waived`)

§§ `18 -- termination by the Senate`

-- s 18(1): the Senate "may by resolution terminate the membership of a member if he or she has been guilty of conduct which in the
-- opinion of the Senate renders him or her unfit to be a member or would bring the Academy into disrepute." (2): it "must not be
-- terminated unless the member concerned has been given an opportunity to give an explanation in writing".
GIVEN `by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN, `conduct unfit or bringing disrepute` IS A BOOLEAN, `given a chance to explain in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the termination is valid` IF
    `by resolution` AND `conduct unfit or bringing disrepute` AND `given a chance to explain in writing`

§§ `22(7) -- obstructing the auditor`

-- s 22(7): "An officer of the Academy who refuses or fails, without any reasonable cause, to allow the Academy's auditor access to any
-- accounting and other records ... or to give any information ... or who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the Academy's auditor
-- ... shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction."
-- "Without any reasonable cause" is attached to refusing or failing; the "otherwise hinders" limb carries no such words.
GIVEN `an officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused or failed access or information` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise hindered the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer commits the section 22(7) offence` IF
        `an officer`
    AND (    (`refused or failed access or information` AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`))
         OR  `otherwise hindered the auditor`)

-- "every day or part of a day" -- the argument counts days and part-days after conviction.
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstructing the auditor` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `26 -- no action against the Academy`

-- s 26(1): "No action shall be maintained against the Academy and the members of the Senate by an advocate and solicitor, lawyer
-- (NP), member, qualified person or eligible person in respect of any act done by the members of the Senate in their official
-- capacity." The bar names its plaintiffs; a person outside those classes is not barred by this section.
DECLARE Plaintiff IS ONE OF
    `an advocate and solicitor`
    `a lawyer (NP)`
    `a member of the Academy`
    `a qualified person`
    `an eligible person`
    `a member of the public`
    `a supplier to the Academy`

GIVEN `the plaintiff` IS A Plaintiff, `an official act of Senate members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is barred by section 26` IF
        `an official act of Senate members`
    AND CONSIDER `the plaintiff`
        WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a supplier to the Academy` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
